* LD2_model.lib -- three interchangeable implementations of the same
* LD2_MODEL subckt (same name + pin interface in every section):
*   ideal  : single ideal inductor, L=4.30n
*   rl     : EM-derived series L+R, L=4.30n R=52.69ohm
*   snp2le : snp2le broadband vector-fitted macromodel (same EM data)
* Select the active one from the including file via:
*   .lib <path>/LD2_model.lib ideal   (or rl, or snp2le)

.lib ideal
.SUBCKT LD2_MODEL p1 p2
L1 p1 p2 4.30n
.ENDS LD2_MODEL
.endl ideal

.lib rl
.SUBCKT LD2_MODEL p1 p2
R1 p1 mid_LD2 52.69
L1 mid_LD2 p2 4.30n
.ENDS LD2_MODEL
.endl rl

.lib snp2le
* LD2_MODEL - lumped-element equivalent (Ngspice / SPICE3)
* generated by snp2le 0.1.18
* EQUIVALENT CIRCUIT FOR VECTOR FITTED S-MATRIX
* Created using scikit-rf vectorFitting.py
* 
* 
* thermal noise of the passive: kT(I - S S^H) at the ports, from a spectral factor of this fit
* sources Rnz_e1..Rnz_e2 (0.25 ohm, the only noisy elements), 8 states nz_x*, controlled sources Gnz_*
* DC pin: Y = Y_fit + dY / (1 + s/wc), fc = 160 Hz, so the model meets the file's 0 Hz point. Nodes dcp_d*, controlled sources Gdcp_*, noiseless
